Package: compositeSS
Type: Package
Title: Design and Sample Size for Estimands That Include Dropout
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jonathan", "Rabinowitz", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "jonathan.rabinowitz@biu.ac.il"),
    person("Ori", "Davidov", role = "ctb"))
Description: Power, sample size, estimation and simulation tools for randomized
    trials in which dropout is treated as part of the outcome (the composite
    strategy of ICH E9(R1)). Implements the expected benefit per randomized
    patient (theta), with closed-form sample size, and the Shih-Quan composite
    test of completion and completers' efficacy, extended to unequal weights,
    a standardized composite effect size (psi) with confidence interval, and a
    contingent (gated) test with recalibrated critical value. Includes
    non-inferiority forms, a dichotomous efficacy option, assurance over prior
    distributions for the planning values, and simulation under random and
    informative (missing not at random) dropout.
